<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica Sept manufacturing output down 1.8 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>SAfrica Sept manufacturing output down 1.8 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African manufacturing production fell 1.8 percent on a seasonally-adjusted basis in September compared with the same month a year ago, the Central Statistical Service (CSS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Month-on-month, seasonally-adjusted manufacturing production was down 3.0 percent.</p>
<p>Index of the physical volume of manufacturing production</p>
<p>(base 1990=100):</p>
<p>				 Sep '96	 Aug '96	Sep '95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  101.9	   105.1	  103.8</p>
<p>    Actual		   106.6	   108.5	  108.5</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
